<title>USA: Burr-Brown Q1 shr drops.</title>
<headline>Burr-Brown Q1 shr drops.</headline>
<dateline>TUCSON, Ariz. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burr-Brown Corp. and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>		     Consolidated Summary of Operations</p>
<p>		  (in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						Three Months Ended:</p>
<p>				     Mar 29,	Dec. 31,    Mar 30,</p>
<p>					 1997	    1996	 1996</p>
<p> Net Revenue		     $54,772	 $50,533    $61,174</p>
<p> Gross margin		     27,372	  25,246     30,677</p>
<p>   % of revenue		    50.0%	   50.0%	50.1%</p>
<p> Research &amp; development	  7,219	   7,364	7,343</p>
<p>Sales, marketing, general</p>
<p>   &amp; administrative	     11,546	  11,175     14,829</p>
<p> Total operating expenses     18,765	  18,539     22,172</p>
<p>   % of revenue		    34.3%	   36.7%	36.2%</p>
<p> Income from operations	  8,607	   6,707	8,505</p>
<p>   % of revenue		    15.7%	   13.3%	13.9%</p>
<p> Other (income)expense	  (781)	   (391)  (7,603)(a)</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p>   income taxes		    9,388	   7,098     16,108</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>   income taxes		    2,816	   1,319	4,510</p>
<p> Net income			  6,572	   5,779  11,598(a)</p>
<p>   % of revenue		    12.0%	   11.4%	19.0%</p>
<p>Shares outstanding</p>
<p>   for EPS		     25,235(b)     24,842(b)  25,397(b)</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>   common share		     0.26	    0.23	 0.46</p>
<p>(a) Includes a gain from the sale of a subsidiary of $6,680 in Other income, $4,810 in Net income and $0.19 in Earnings per</p>
<p>common share. (b) Reflects a 3 for 2 stock split effective April, 1997.</p>
</text>
